<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $43.6 mln April 8.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $43.6 mln April 8.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $43.6 million surplus on April 9 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 8</p>
<p>Exports: $156.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $239.2 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $341.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $215.6 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $43.6 million</p>
<p>ARPIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.082 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.247 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.371 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.265 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $59 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
